/*!
 * Vernier — static/js/engine.js
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Dependency-free math expression engine for the scientific and graphing modes.
 *
 *   tokenizer  ->  recursive-descent parser  ->  ast  ->  evaluator
 *
 * No eval(), no new Function(), no modules, no build step. Classic script that
 * publishes a single global: window.CalcEngine (also usable from a worker or a
 * headless sandbox via the factory returned at the bottom of the IIFE).
 *
 * The engine is deliberately UI-agnostic: it knows nothing about the DOM, the
 * keypad, or the canvas. It only turns text into numbers and numbers into text.
 *
 * Public surface
 *   CalcEngine.tokenize(source)                     -> [{type,value,pos}, ...]
 *   CalcEngine.parse(source, options)               -> ast
 *   CalcEngine.evaluate(sourceOrAst, options)       -> number   (throws on error)
 *   CalcEngine.compile(source, options)             -> function (x) => number
 *   CalcEngine.sample(expressions, xMin, xMax, n, options)
 *                                                   -> [[x, y|null], ...]
 *                                                      or [curve, curve] for an array input
 *   CalcEngine.format(value, options)               -> display string
 *   CalcEngine.getAngleMode() / setAngleMode(mode)  -> "DEG" | "RAD"
